\looseness=-1 Table~\ref{tab:proxy_comparison} compares four candidate uncertainty proxies against $K{=}10$ sample variance as ground truth. CRM correction magnitude (the $L_2$ norm of the CRM's predicted residual) is attractive because it requires no extra VLA forward passes, but correlates weakly with true uncertainty ($\rho < 0.16$): the CRM predicts similar-magnitude corrections regardless of whether the VLA is confident or uncertain. FMVD, which measures dispersion in the flow-matching velocity field, performs worse still ($\rho{=}0.083$). The $K{=}2$ pairwise $L_2$ distance achieves near-perfect correlation ($\rho{=}0.9979$) at the cost of one additional VLA forward pass, which is absorbed by batched inference (Section~\ref{sec:efficiency}).

